<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anton Florian, Prince of Liechtenstein</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1656">1656</a>–<a href="/years/1721">1721</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anton Florian was prince of Liechtenstein from 1718 to 1721. A courtier and diplomat who had been tutor to the future Emperor Charles VI, he obtained from Charles in 1719 the union of Vaduz and Schellenberg as the Imperial Principality of Liechtenstein, the state that still bears the family name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anton-florian-prince-of-liechtenstein.jpg" alt="Anton Florian, Prince of Liechtenstein" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anton_Florian_v_Liechtenstein.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
